course: dictionary
lesson: 4819
title: One word, many meanings: hungry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word hungry has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The simplest meaning is about food: feeling that you need to eat. «Being hungry makes it harder to think and learn in the afternoon.» Here your body is sending a signal that it needs energy.
explain: Hungry can also mean wanting something very much, as in «hungry for success». Nobody is eating anything there; the word shows strong desire. Ask yourself: is there food in this sentence, or is someone eager for something else?
explain: Hungry can also describe people who do not have enough food, as in «go hungry». Writers use stronger words like «starving» or «as hungry as a wolf» to show very great hunger. «I'm starving» said three and a half hours after a full school lunch usually means «I'm quite hungry», so even an exaggeration needs context to understand.
fact: Hungry is an adjective, and its other forms are hungrier and hungriest.
fact: Hungry means feeling that you need or want to eat.
fact: «Hungry for» means eager for something, such as «hungry for success».
fact: «Go hungry» means not having enough food.
fact: «Starving» and «as hungry as a wolf» show very great hunger.
exercise: «The bears woke up thin and hungry in spring.» What does hungry mean here? | Full of energy and ready to race | Cold to touch | Angry with the other bears | *Needing food after a long winter sleep
exercise: «She is hungry for success.» What does hungry mean here? | She is tired of school | *She wants success very much | She has not eaten all day | Hungry for a sandwich
exercise: Some families go hungry when there is not enough money for food. What does go hungry mean? | *Not have enough food | Have a big meal at a restaurant | Skip playtime to finish work | Walk a long way to school
test: «Being hungry makes it harder to think and learn.» Which meaning of hungry is used here? | *Feeling that you need to eat | Being very rude | Wanting something very much | Having no food at all in the country
test: «A child who is hungry finds it hard to keep calm.» Why does this matter? | *Hunger is the body's signal that it needs food, and it makes calm and learning harder | Hungry means always cross | Children should never eat lunch | Hungry is a kind of sport
exam: Which sentence uses hungry to mean wanting something very much? | Hungry children need food | I am hungry after my swim | The bears are hungry in spring | *The young writer is hungry for praise
